msgid "Unset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:103
msgid ""
"Absolute path to a custom ``AppRun`` file.  The file is copied to the top "
"level of the AppDir and made executable, taking precedence over both the "
"generated ``AppRun`` and an ``AppRun`` installed by the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:111
msgid ""
"Embed the value of this variable as the update information.  See the "
"``appimagetool`` source code for the supported values and formats of the ``--"
"updateinformation`` option.  It is highly recommended to have the "
"``zsyncmake`` tool installed if using ``zsync`` update information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:120
msgid ""
"When this variable is true, add the ``--guess`` option to the "
"``appimagetool`` invocation.  This directs the tool to try to guess "
"appropriate update information based on GitHub or GitLab environment "
"variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:129
msgid ""
"Override the ``appimagetool``'s default type of squashfs compression (zstd). "
"This corresponds to the ``appimagetool --comp`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:136
msgid ""
"List of arguments to pass through to ``mksquashfs``.  Each of these will be "
"preceded by ``--mksquashfs-opt`` on the ``appimagetool`` command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:143
msgid ""
"If set to true, do not check AppStream metadata.  This passes the ``--no-"
"appstream`` option to ``appimagetool``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:150
msgid ""
"Use the specified file as an exclude file for ``mksquashfs``, in addition to "
"``.appimageignore``.  This uses the ``--exclude-file`` option to "
"``appimagetool``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:158
msgid ""
"Specify a runtime file to use instead of letting the ``appimagetool`` "
"download a runtime to embed in the generated AppImage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:165
msgid ""
"When set to true, sign the generated AppImage with "
"gpg[2]. :variable:`CPACK_APPIMAGE_SIGN_KEY` should also be specified if "
"using this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:173
msgid ""
"Key ID to use for gpg[2] signatures when signing is enabled "
"with :variable:`CPACK_APPIMAGE_SIGN`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:182
msgid ""
"If the :variable:`CPACK_APPIMAGE_SIGN_KEY` is encrypted and requires a "
"passphrase to be used for signing (and, for some reason, GnuPG cannot be "
"used interactively, e.g., in a CI environment), this environment variable "
"can be used to safely pass the key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:193
msgid ""
"Architecture of the AppImage, passed to ``appimagetool`` in the ``ARCH`` "
"environment variable.  The :module:`CPack` module derives it from "
"the :variable:`CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR` of the project, so it matches the "
"target when cross-compiling.  The supported values are ``x86_64``, ``i686``, "
"``aarch64``, and ``armhf``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:199
msgid ""
"It needs to be set when the processor cannot be mapped to one of those "
"values and ``appimagetool`` cannot automatically determine the architecture "
"of the binaries inside the AppDir to choose a suitable runtime (e.g., when "
"binaries for multiple architectures or just shell scripts are contained in "
"there)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:205
msgid "Derived from :variable:`CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR` on Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:211
msgid "This value will be inserted by appimagetool into the root desktop file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cpack_gen/appimage.rst:213
msgid ":variable:`CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION`"
msgstr ""
